 \"l11\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-0bba10627d55bbfd09470f5c\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/connect-network/congress-archive\", \"text\": \"Toggle navigation dropdown Congress archive\", \"source_region\": \"navigation\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 392, \"end\": 572, \"text\": \"Innovation\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEHA2026 Congress\\nCongress archive\\nScientific meetings\\nMembership\\nEHA2027 registration\\nEHA2027 program\\nEHA2027 abstract submission\\nEHA2027\"}}], \"supported_parent_doc_ids\": [], \"source_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-0bba10627d55bbfd09470f5c\", \"title\": \"EHA Advanced Research Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Advanced Research Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4058, \"end\": 4085, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 27}, {\"start\": 4148, \"end\": 4203, \"excerpt_start\": 28, \"excerpt_end\": 83}, {\"start\": 4453, \"end\": 5971, \"excerpt_start\": 84, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Advanced Research Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n2 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nThe EHA Advanced Research Grant is a type of EHA Research Grant, which can provide up to €240,000 for three years.\\nEligibility\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nYou’re an EHA member\\nYour institute is an academic research center or proven equivalent in Europe\\nYou have the support of an academic department and institute\\nYour application relates to basic and translational lab-based research in hematology\\nYour application will not be eligible if it relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\\nSpecific criteria for the EHA Advanced Research Grant\\nOur Advanced Research Grant is suitable for researchers who:\\nAre currently carrying out basic or translational lab-based research in hematology\\nReceived a PhD or PharmD less than eight years before the closing date listed above\\nHave at least one first author publication\\nIf you received your PhD or PharmD outside of this timeframe, please check our policy on life events. If this policy applies to you, you can ask us to extend the period of eligibility.\\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Advanced Research Grant’ on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in countries less-represented among EHA gra\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-ece509e1ea7055ce41222f0b\", \"title\": \"Non-EHA funding opportunities - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Non-EHA funding opportunities - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4130, \"end\": 4185, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 55}, {\"start\": 4407, \"end\": 4690, \"excerpt_start\": 56, \"excerpt_end\": 339}, {\"start\": 5152, \"end\": 5172, \"excerpt_start\": 340, \"excerpt_end\": 360}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n1 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nOn this page, we’ll list other interesting funding opportunities for European researchers in hematology.\\nIf you’d like us to add any opportunity to this page, please contact [email protected].\\nCurrent opportunities:\\nDKMS John Hansen Research Grant\\nShare\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-8cc45db4f74ca26842ee7011\", \"title\": \"Extending the reach of EHA Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Extending the reach of EHA Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4082, \"end\": 4115, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 33}, {\"start\": 4204, \"end\": 4259, \"excerpt_start\": 34, \"excerpt_end\": 89}, {\"start\": 4435, \"end\": 4958, \"excerpt_start\": 90, \"excerpt_end\": 613}, {\"start\": 5374, \"end\": 5394, \"excerpt_start\": 614, \"excerpt_end\": 634}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Extending the reach of EHA Grants\\nLeft Sidebar\\n1 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nTo ensure our whole community benefits from funding opportunities, we’ve created opportunities across diverse grants categories for researchers based in countries less-represented among EHA grantees.\\nThe eligible countries are:\\nAlbania\\nArmenia\\nAzerbaijan\\nBosnia and Herzegovina\\nBulgaria\\nCroatia\\nEstonia\\nGeorgia\\nHungary\\nKosovo\\nLatvia\\nLithuania\\nMoldova\\nMontenegro\\nNorth Macedonia\\nPoland\\nPortugal\\nRomania\\nSerbia\\nSlovakia\\nSlovenia\\nTürkiye\\nUkraine\\nEHA Research Grants\\nEHA Kick-off Grants\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grants\\nShare\\nBecome an EHA Mentor\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-5ea6489c02f2281589b4de8a\", \"title\": \"EHA Research Grant review and selection process - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Research Grant review and selection process - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4240, \"end\": 4295, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 55}, {\"start\": 4471, \"end\": 6016, \"excerpt_start\": 56, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n5 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nEHA Research Grant review and selection process\\nApplicants will receive updates at each stage of the process and, where possible, feedback on their application.\\nStep 1: Eligibility check\\nAfter the deadline has passed, we’ll check your application for completion and compliance with the eligibility criteria.\\nWe will not review applications that:\\nAre incomplete—for example, that are missing signatures or do not include a budget\\nDo not meet the eligibility criteria\\nIf your application did not qualify for review, you’ll receive a notification. This decision is final.\\nStep 2: Preliminary Review\\nEHA’s Fellowships and Grants Committee will:\\nPerform a preliminary review of the applications\\nDecide which applications will proceed to the next stage, which is an in-depth evaluation by an external peer review panel\\nYou’ll receive a notification about the success of your application in this first round. If you have not been selected for the next round, you’ll receive short feedback from the Committee.\\nStep 3: External review\\nTo assist our Fellowships and Grants Committee with the selection procedure, at least three external reviewers will review the project proposal in detail. These reviewers will be experts in the proposal’s topic.\\nExternal reviewers will score your application based on the following parameters.\\nProject\\nThe significance and impact.\\nThe novelty and originality.\\nThe appropriateness of the methods.\\nThe feasibility of the proposal.\\nThe host institute/scientific environment where the research will be conducted.\\nInvestigat\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-6e910e647f1ecc56f921759d\", \"title\": \"2023 winners - The European Hematology Association (EHA)2023 winners - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4069, \"end\": 4124, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 55}, {\"start\": 4229, \"end\": 5774, \"excerpt_start\": 56, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n7 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\n2023 winners\\nJunior Research Grant\\nAttya Omer\\nTopic: Advanced engineering of hematopoietic stem cells and bone marrow niche, toward next generation gene therapy Ospedale San Raffaele Italy\\nMarino Caruso\\nTopic: Translatome analysis of cancer associated ribosomal protein mutations KU Leuven Belgium\\nNadia El Khawanky\\nTopic: The role of RNA and DNA sensing pathways in AML for the development of anti-leukemic immunity Klinikum Rechts der Isar Germany\\nAdvanced Research Grant\\nAdam Wilkinson\\nTopi